  "raw": {
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/glenvilleedu/jobs/5259451/gsu-student-position-pioneer-support-mentor-tutor": {
      "title": "GSU Student Position: Pioneer Support Mentor/Tutor",
      "description": "GSU Student Position: Pioneer Support Mentor/Tutor Salary $8.75 Hourly Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485TWS0037Z Division Academic Center Opening Date 03/05/2026 Description Pioneer Support is looking for Mentors to provide in-person and virtual tutoring. Mentors must have experience in professional communication and have excellent customer services skills. Additionally, Mentors must be knowledgeable in the resources and services that Pioneer Support and Glenville State University offers. We are looking for students who are majoring in or have completed coursework in Criminal Justice OR Business, Examples of Duties Meet with students in a one-to-one or small-group basis to integrate learning strategies that address problem areas and promote independent learning. Maintain a weekly schedule of available hours in Pioneer Support for drop-in tutoring appointments. Ensure coordination and documentation of tutoring sessions by using the Penji scheduling platform. Attend orientation and training sessions as required by Pioneer Support staff. Assist with additional duties as needed, e.g., covering front desk, answering phones, organizing materials, organizing the computer lab, performing other clerical duties, etc. Make appropriate referrals to other campus resources and promptly inform Pioneer Support staff of any developments. Conduct light cleaning as necessary. Support all tutoring center policies. Complete Tutor Certification Process (if applicable). Typical Qualifications Cumulative GPA of at least 3.0 in content area. Recommendation from an instructor in content area preferred. Good interpersonal communication skills and ease in relating to people from varying educational, cultural, and social backgrounds. Ability to maintain confidential student information and sign an agreement as to such. Responsibility, reliability, and punctuality. Appropriate and professional behavior at all times. Current enrollment as a GSU student. Supplemental Information Applicants must include a letter of interest, current resume/employment application, and names and contact information for at least three references. Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm . Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Women, members of minorities and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/glenvilleedu/jobs/5260097/security-officer-part-time": {
      "title": "Security Officer- Part Time",
      "description": "Security Officer- Part Time Salary $16.00 Hourly Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485T00023Z Division Public Safety Opening Date 03/05/2026 Description Glenville State University has an immediate opening for a Part-time Security Guard with no state benefits. The applicant may work up to, but not exceed, 1040 hours annually. The Security Guard position reports to the Director of Public Safety. The primary purpose for this position is to provide and maintain a safe and secure environment for Faculty, Staff, Students and Visitors at Glenville State University by providing a variety of security services. The position provides a visible, mobile presence throughout the entire campus to ensure all persons accomplish their educational and business objectives. Examples of Duties Patrol all areas on campus for the purpose of reducing and preventing personal harm and destruction of property. Check all buildings for security, fire and safety violations. Report all deficiencies in a timely manner and correct minor infractions whenever possible. Patrol campus during special events which draw large crowds and direct traffic in order to prevent congestion. Provide crowd control including subduing disruptive persons. Enforce all applicable college rules, regulations and policies. Assist all local agencies responding to emergencies on campus property. Monitor parking in all campus lots and issue citations when violations are identified. Become familiar with all aspects of crisis response and follow appropriate action as needed. Assist the Director of Public Safety with required training programs including safety, security and emergency. Typical Qualifications A High School Diploma or GED is required. No experience required but at least six months related experience preferred. Basic computer skills. Applicant needs to be equipped with good verbal and written communication skills and an ability to relate with young adults. Background knowledge of GSU rules, regulations and policies is preferred. Individual must have a valid driver's license and be able and willing to work a rotating schedule. Willing to undergo Self-defense tactics training. Willing to undergo Oleoresin Capsicum (OC) spray training. Physical/Work Demands : Requires long periods of standing, walking, bending and lifting up to 50 lbs., running, jumping, climbing, and physical interaction with public. Patrols campus on foot daily and during special events. Supplemental Information Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm or by email at hr@glenville.edu . Screening of all applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Minorities, women, and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/glenvilleedu/jobs/5325492/chief-financial-officer-vice-president-of-business-finance": {
      "title": "Chief Financial Officer / Vice President of Business & Finance",
      "description": "Chief Financial Officer / Vice President of Business & Finance Salary $120,000.00 Annually Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485P00147S Division President's Office Opening Date 04/29/2026 Description Benefits Description Reporting to the President, the Chief Financial Officer (CFO) creates and establishes yearly financial objectives that align with GSU's overall enrollment and other operating plans and long term strategy. This individual serves as a member of the President’s Cabinet and works collaboratively with fellow Cabinet members to set and pursue goals and strategies to advance the mission and strategy of the University. The CFO interacts and collaborates effectively with other departmental leadership, academic leaders, and athletic staff to create a shared commitment and active participation in achieving the University's strategic initiatives and financial goals. The Chief Financial Officer primarily supervises staff in the business office including Accountants, Cashier's office, the Controller and other Financial Professional staff, procurement personnel, administrative professionals, and student workers. Supervision of other departments and areas may be assigned based on previous supervisory background and work experience. ABOUT GLENVILLE STATE UNIVERSITY: Glenville State University is a small public college located in the scenic, central region of West Virginia. Founded in 1872 as a normal school, Glenville State currently prepares students for careers in teaching, business, land resources, fine arts, criminal justice, nursing and health sciences, all grounded in a liberal arts core curriculum. GSU also offers graduate programs in Education and will begin offering further graduate options in Business and Criminal Justice beginning in the Fall, 2023. With an enrollment of approximately 1,000+ on-campus students, the University offers masters, baccalaureate and associate degrees. The University's enrollment is composed primarily of first-generation and moderate-income students, largely from within the State of West Virginia. Examples of Duties The appointment carries specific duties and responsibilities: Assess and evaluate financial performance in regard to long and short term operational goals, budgets, and forecasts. Prepare and review monthly financial reports and provide recommendations. Supervise the accounting department and financial systems. Regularly review and ensure application of appropriate internal controls and compliance therewith. Prepare/present periodic budget-to-actual reports. Prepare the annual budget and periodic forecasting. Assure regular maintenance and backup of all accounting systems. Ensure timeliness and accuracy of financial data reports. Oversee the preparation and timely filing of all local, state, and federal tax returns. Meet all information and reporting requirements from the HEPC, other State authorities, and other governing entities. Work with Human Resources to ensure appropriate legal compliance. Serve as key point of contact for external auditors; manage preparation and support of all external audits. Manage cash flow planning process and ensure funds availability for operational and capital needs. Manage financial planning and analysis including creating reports, and related analysis. Assist in the oversight of institutional grant administration. Oversee student billing and collection, including Cashier's Office. May include supervision of other non-financial departments. Review and provide recommendation regarding all university contracts. Serve as Chief Procurement Officer, ensuring compliance with all state purchasing and payment policies and procedures. Other duties as assigned by the President. Typical Qualifications An MBA or similar degree is required. Qualified candidates will have a minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible experience in financial management, preferably within higher education. The successful candidate will demonstrate respect for a diverse academic environment of students, faculty, and staff with varying social, economic, cultural, ideological, and ethnic views and experiences, and will exercise the ability to: Develop and maintain relationships and strategic alliances with vendors and business partners. Recommend and engage consultants, auditors, and investors as needed. Develop budgets and related financial data and projections and communicate results and recommendations to the President, Board of Governors and senior staff. Participate in key decisions as they relate to strategic initiatives and operational models. Candidates seeking this outstanding opportunity will also possess: Strong technology skills, including experience with web-based systems critical to the College (WV Oasis, and Banner). Proficient knowledge of financial accounting and reporting standards. Familiarity with financial records, data analysis, and assessment. Strong business process experience with the ability to ensure efficiencies and effectiveness among Business Office functions. Public speaking and strong writing skills. Proven budget management. Managerial skills. Willingness and ability to travel, work evenings and weekends, as necessary. Supplemental Information Applicants must include a letter of interest, current resume/employment application, and names and contact information for at least three references.Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm or by email at hr@glenville.edu . Screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Women, members of minorities and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. As an agency of State government, Glenville State University provides a wide variety of benefits to its employees. Some benefits are mandatory to both the college and employees, while some benefits are elective by employees. Some benefits are free to employees while some benefits require employee contributions. Current year details regarding plan options and monthly premium costs can be obtained by logging onto the PEIA Web site at www.wvpeia.com or by contacting the GSU payroll department. Life Insurance: $10,000 free to employees, optional coverage up to $500,000 based on age and salary. Additional plans are available for spouse and child coverage. Accidental Death Insurance: Optional employee or family plan of $25,000 to $100,000. For details contact the payroll department. Retirement Plan: The college matches your 6 percent contribution (tax exempt dollars) towards TIAA/CREF or Teacher's Retirement System. Thus, 12 percent of your gross salary is working for your retirement income. New employees must join TIAA/CREF. TIAA Total Disability Benefits Plan: Optional employees coverage that provides (1) monthly income and (2) payments of premiums to your TIAA/CREF retirement plan to participating employees who suffer total, long-term disabilities. The cost is adjusted according to individual salary on a yearly basis. Employees become eligible upon completion of the first year of employment. Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/glenvilleedu/jobs/5336555/gsu-student-position-reading-math-tutor": {
      "title": "GSU Student Position- Reading/Math Tutor",
      "description": "GSU Student Position- Reading/Math Tutor Salary $8.75 Hourly Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485TWS016z Division Financial Aid Opening Date 05/08/2026 Description As required by federal regulations, the University must employ at least one work-study eligible student per academic year to work as a reading tutor for children who are preschool age or are in elementary school. The University must also employ a mathematics tutor for elementary children. Federal work-study eligibility is required for this position. If you are uncertain if you qualify for work-study funding, please check with a Financial Aid staff member to ensure that you are eligible before applying. Examples of Duties The reading and math student tutor(s) will be employed by the GSU Financial Aid Office, in collaboration with Gilmer County Elementary School. The tutor(s) report directly to the Financial Aid Office Assistant II and indirectly to the Director of Financial Aid. The primary expectations and duties of the tutor are as follows: Be approachable and respectful to elementary school teachers, staff, and students Act responsibly and abide by all GSU and county school policies and procedures Be proficient in the area(s) for which the University student will tutor Assist students with homework, projects, test preparation, writing papers, research, or other academic tasks as assigned by the elementary school teachers or staff Ability to work with students to help them understand key concepts Ability to teach skills to improve academic performance, including study strategies, note-taking skills, and approaches to answering test questions Ability to provide students positive and constructive feedback Typical Qualifications Minimum 2.50 cumulative GPA required, cumulative 3.0 or above preferred Education major and observation hours completed preferred Ability to maintain confidential student information Interpersonal communication/customer service skills Appropriate dress and professional behavior required Current enrollment as a GSU student Supplemental Information Applicants must include a letter of interest, current resume/employment application, and names and contact information for at least three references. Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm . Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Women, members of minorities and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/glenvilleedu/jobs/5341864/part-time-maintenance-worker": {
      "title": "Part time Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "Part time Maintenance Worker Salary $12.00 Hourly Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485T00001Z Division Physical Plant Opening Date 05/13/2026 Description This is a part-time, temporary, nonexempt position which is a pay grade 2 on the salary schedule. The primary purpose of this position is to assist tradesmen and other facilities staff in all aspects of physical plant operations including facilities and grounds maintenance. Examples of Duties Ability to read and follow instructions. Must be skilled with the use of common tools and equipment used in various trades associated with Physical Plant operations. Must be able to strip and wax floors and move furniture. Mowing and weed eating are some other duties that may be required. Basic math and computer skills are a must. Must have the initiative to work alone and proceed with assigned task. Scheduled shift may vary Typical Qualifications Reliable, dependable and must show up for work on time as scheduled. Position requires ability to lift objects 25-50 pounds and willingness to work in adverse conditions. Supplemental Information Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm or by email at hr@glenville.edu . Screening of all applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Glenville State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/glenvilleedu/jobs/5479758/gsu-student-position-student-activities-board-member": {
      "title": "GSU Student Position- Student Activities Board Member",
      "description": "GSU Student Position- Student Activities Board Member Salary $8.75 Hourly Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485TWS025 Division Student Life Opening Date 09/11/2026 Description The Office of Student Life is seeking a variety of student workers to be key members of the campus life and engagement team. As a member of the Student Activities Board, students will engage with the student body to help both plan and implement a wide variety of events on behalf of the Office of Student Life. The events will be both standalone events and collaborative events with other campus offices and student organizations. The Student Activities Board members will represent the interests of the entire GSU student body while getting hands on experience in communication, budgeting, marketing, and interpersonal relationships. Examples of Duties Assist with setup, breakdown, registration, and hosting of campus events (Homecoming, movie nights, guest speakers, tournaments, social activities, and more). Participate in required team meetings and brainstorming sessions to foster unique event ideas that promotes a vibrant campus culture. Create promotional materials, assist with social media outreach, and distribute flyers across campus to boost student attendance. Serve as a friendly, approachable representative of the Office of Student Life and the Student Activities Board to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Help maintain, organize, and store event supplies and equipment. Maintain student confidentiality when handling event sign-ins and abide by all University and Student Life policies and procedures. Typical Qualifications Currently enrolled as a degree-seeking GSU student. Minimum 2.50 cumulative GPA required; 3.0 or higher preferred. Strong interpersonal communication, customer service, and teamwork skills. Punctual, proactive, and capable of managing event logistics while maintaining professional behavior and appropriate attire. Willingness to work evening and weekend hours based on the event schedule. Prior experience in event planning, graphic design, social media marketing, or student leadership preferred but not required. While prior experience isn’t required, enthusiasm is. Along with your application, please include a letter stating why you would like to be a member of the Student Activities Board. Supplemental Information Applicants must include a letter of interest, current resume/employment application, and names and contact information for at least three references. Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm . Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Women, members of minorities and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/glenvilleedu/jobs/5507161/financial-controller": {
      "title": "Financial Controller",
      "description": "Financial Controller Salary $85,000.00 Annually Location 200 High Street, Glenville, WV Job Type Non-classified Job Number 0485P00148S Division Business and Finance Opening Date 10/06/2026 Description Benefits Description The Controller directs, manages, supervises, plans, and coordinates all activities and operations of an institution's major accounting divisions. Responsible for preparation of recurring and ad hoc financial reporting and related analysis work to support decision making for the institution. Examples of Duties The Controller is responsible for overseeing and coordinating the institution's day to day financial affairs in all major accounting divisions including: payroll and benefits, accounts payable and receivable, revenue collections, student loan collections, and external and internal financial reporting. Maintain the Universities Accounting system (Banner), schedule and review recurring and ad hoc financial reports, review and approve purchase requisitions, maintain policies and procedures, direct production of monthly, quarterly and annual financial reports, Final approval of all OASIS (State accounting system) documents. Responsible for coordination of the university's financial system with the state system. Additional responsibilities include supervising and directing the work activities of accountants as well as other financial supporting staff assigned to the unit. Job responsibilities require advance knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP) and practices, in addition to auditing principles, financial reporting, accounting regulations and internal controls. Work is performed independently, by applying established standards through a broad and deep knowledge base of work acquired from several years of experience in this professional field. Problems faced in this position are varied, often complex, and involve multiple constituencies, often with competing priorities. Decisions have significant, broad implications for the management and operations of a division/entire institution as well as contribute to decisions on the overall strategy and direction of the entire institution. Typical Qualifications The candidate needs knowledge of accounting systems, internal controls and would preferably have experience in higher education, and non-profit. Degree in Accounting, Business Administration, Finance, or related field is required and CPA or advanced business degree preferred, with a minimum of 4 years supervisory experience and a \"team-first\" attitude, plus personal and professional skills for a management level position. Supplemental Information Applicants must include a letter of interest, current resume/employment application, and names and contact information for at least three references. Apply online at http://agency.governmentjobs.com/glenvilleedu/default.cfm or by email at hr@glenville.edu. Screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Glenville State University is proud of its commitment to affirmative action. Women, members of minorities and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. As an agency of State government, Glenville State University provides a wide variety of benefits to its employees. Some benefits are mandatory to both the college and employees, while some benefits are elective by employees. Some benefits are free to employees while some benefits require employee contributions. Current year details regarding plan options and monthly premium costs can be obtained by logging onto the PEIA Web site at www.wvpeia.com or by contacting the GSU payroll department. Life Insurance: $10,000 free to employees, optional coverage up to $500,000 based on age and salary. Additional plans are available for spouse and child coverage. Accidental Death Insurance: Optional employee or family plan of $25,000 to $100,000. For details contact the payroll department. Retirement Plan: The college matches your 6 percent contribution (tax exempt dollars) towards TIAA/CREF or Teacher's Retirement System. Thus, 12 percent of your gross salary is working for your retirement income. New employees must join TIAA/CREF. TIAA Total Disability Benefits Plan: Optional employees coverage that provides (1) monthly income and (2) payments of premiums to your TIAA/CREF retirement plan to participating employees who suffer total, long-term disabilities. The cost is adjusted according to individual salary on a yearly basis. Employees become eligible upon completion of the first year of employment. Employer Glenville State University Address 200 High Street Glenville, West Virginia, 26351 Phone (304) 462-6193 Website http://www.glenville.edu Apply"
    }
